  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want a modern theme and a retro green-on-black terminal theme, so that I can give the app a look other than the classic one.\n\nOperator request of 2026-10-28: « Thème Swift » (light/dark, the design language of the operator's other app) and « Thème rétro » (« as400 »: terminal font, green text, black background). M4.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #729\n- #842\n\n### Scope\n\nTwo `theme.json` themes for the LOT-188 engine ([`docs/THEMES.md`](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/THEMES.md) §3, §6):\n\n- **Swift** (light, dark), family Classiques: tokens from the operator's design language (cards, halos, gradient used sparingly). Values **to be confirmed with the operator** (the board `theme-swift.jpg` and `docs/assets/themes/tokens/themes.json` show the 2026-10-28 values); no code or asset is copied from the other app.\n- **Rétro 5250** (single variant), family Rétro, named after IBM 5250 green-screen terminals with no trademark in the name (operator Q9): monospace everywhere (system `.monospaced` design, no new font), green phosphor on black, reverse-video selection, square corners; a blinking cursor only without Reduce Motion.\n\n### Legacy counterpart\n\nNone @ 87fe0d1c. Covered by LOT-188's GAP row.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-188 (#?)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Contrast test green for both themes (every pair of THEMES.md §3).\n- [ ] Rétro 5250 checked at Dynamic Type AX5 (monospace wraps, nothing clipped) and in the reader (`[code]` still distinct from body text).\n- [ ] Screenshots light/dark (Swift) and single (Rétro) of the forum list and a topic page in the PR, no real pseudo.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green; UI strings in French; no new dependency; authors in CREDITS.md.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/THEMES.md §8 (submitting a theme), the LOT-188 spec. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR body `LOT-192`, `Closes #<this issue>`, `Claim: <session-id>`.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
